IMPORT prelude

-- Statutory Declarations Act 1959 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1959A00052.txt
-- (compilation No. 8, 1 January 2024). The declarant asks: "Is my statutory
-- declaration validly made; can it be used for what I want; what if a
-- statement in it is false?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 8: the two ways a declaration is made.
DECLARE `How made` IS ONE OF
    `signed under the observation of a prescribed person`
    `completed and signed on an approved online platform`
    `neither`

-- s 9(b).
DECLARE `Observation` IS ONE OF
    `in person`
    `by video link`

-- s 7A(1).
DECLARE `Signature` IS ONE OF
    `by hand on a physical form`
    `by electronic means on an electronic form`
    `otherwise`

-- s 6(2)-(3).
DECLARE `Use` IS ONE OF
    `for the purposes of, or a matter under, a Commonwealth or Territory law`
    `in the administration of a Commonwealth Department`
    `as evidence in a judicial proceeding`
    `another use`

DECLARE `Declaration case` HAS
    `it is in the approved form`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `how it was made`                                               IS A `How made`
    -- s 7A
    `how I signed`                                                  IS A `Signature`
    `the method identifies me and shows my intention`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the method was appropriately reliable or proven in fact`       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9
    `I was observed`                                                IS A `Observation`
    `the prescribed person signed the declaration`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prescribed person signed a copy they were satisfied was true` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9A(1)(b)-(c)
    `my identity was verified by an approved identity service as prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it includes the platform information the regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 6
    `the use I want`                                                IS A `Use`
    `the law shows a contrary intention`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 11
    `I intentionally made a false statement in it`                  IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Declaration position` HAS
    `my declaration is validly made`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `this Act authorises the use`                                   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `I commit an offence under s 11`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum imprisonment in years`                                 IS A NUMBER

§ `Rules`

-- s 7A: a valid signature by hand or electronically.
@ref s 7A
GIVEN c IS A `Declaration case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is validly signed` c IF
        NOT (c's `how I signed` EQUALS `otherwise`)
    AND c's `the method identifies me and shows my intention`
    AND c's `the method was appropriately reliable or proven in fact`

-- s 9(c): the prescribed person signs the declaration, or, observing by video
-- link, a copy they are satisfied is a true copy.
@ref s 9
GIVEN c IS A `Declaration case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9 is met` c IF
        c's `how it was made` EQUALS `signed under the observation of a prescribed person`
    AND (   c's `the prescribed person signed the declaration`
         OR (    c's `I was observed` EQUALS `by video link`
             AND c's `the prescribed person signed a copy they were satisfied was true`))

@ref s 9A(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Declaration case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9A is met` c IF
        c's `how it was made` EQUALS `completed and signed on an approved online platform`
    AND c's `my identity was verified by an approved identity service as prescribed`
    AND c's `it includes the platform information the regulations prescribe`

-- s 8: in the approved form, signed (s 7A), and made under s 9 or s 9A.
@ref ss 7A, 8, 9, 9A
GIVEN c IS A `Declaration case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is validly made` c IF
        c's `it is in the approved form`
    AND `it is validly signed` c
    AND (`section 9 is met` c OR `section 9A is met` c)

-- s 6(2): usable for a Commonwealth or Territory law, unless a contrary
-- intention appears, and in a Department's administration. s 6(3): it does not
-- authorise use as evidence in a judicial proceeding (though it does not
-- prevent it). Changed after the independent pass.
@ref s 6
GIVEN c IS A `Declaration case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`does the Act authorise the use for` c MEANS
    IF NOT (`it is validly made` c)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER c's `the use I want`
         WHEN `for the purposes of, or a matter under, a Commonwealth or Territory law` THEN JUST (NOT (c's `the law shows a contrary intention`))
         WHEN `in the administration of a Commonwealth Department` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `as evidence in a judicial proceeding` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `another use` THEN JUST FALSE

-- s 11: intentionally making a false statement; imprisonment for 4 years.
@ref s 11
GIVEN c IS A `Declaration case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I commit an offence` c IF c's `I intentionally made a false statement in it`

@ref ss 6-11
@export default The position of a person making a Commonwealth statutory declaration under the Statutory Declarations Act 1959 (Cth): whether it is validly made (in the approved form, signed by hand or electronically by a reliable method that identifies the declarant, and either signed under a prescribed person's observation in person or by video link and signed by that person or a true copy signed by them, or completed on an approved online platform with identity verified by an approved identity service: ss 7A-9A); whether the Act authorises the use the declarant wants (for a Commonwealth or Territory law unless it shows a contrary intention, or a Department's administration; the Act neither authorises nor prevents use as evidence in court: s 6); and whether intentionally making a false statement in it is an offence (s 11: imprisonment for 4 years). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Declaration case`  @desc The form, how it was made and signed, the observation or verification, the use I want, and whether a statement was knowingly false
GIVETH A `Declaration position`
`the declaration position for` c MEANS
    `Declaration position` OF `it is validly made` c, `does the Act authorise the use for` c, `I commit an offence` c,
                              (IF `I commit an offence` c THEN 4 ELSE 0)
